  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nThere is a Synapse which started returning 200 OK for PUT messages when sending messages but the messages have stopped persisting into the room. Synapse has been restarted since. When sending messages in a fresh session (in Element), the messages get persisted.\r\n\r\n> 2020-11-16 08:03:55,336 - synapse.access.http.8008 - 311 - INFO - PUT-9787- 1.2.3.4 - 8008 - {@user:xxxxxxx.ems.host} Processed request: 0.005sec/-0.000sec (0.004sec, 0.000sec) (0.001sec/0.001sec/1) 59B 200 \"PUT /_matrix/client/r0/rooms/!BCoxxxxxxx:xxxxxxxxxx.ems.host/send/m.room.message/1164?access_token=<redacted> HTTP/1.1\" \"Net::Async::Matrix\" [0 dbevts]\r\n\r\nThe client sending the messages is Matrixmon. Have verified the messages do not end up in the `events` table either.\r\n\r\nI have the credentials for the account for the problematic session which can be used to reproduce locally.\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\nEMS hosted Synapse v1.22.1",
